# Corpus unit self-expansion/C04 — gap (policy-mandatory variance + scope CQs unmet)
#
# Source: self-expansion C04 annotation (generalization, component_substitution;
# corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: SEMA generalises across functional adapter types -- swapping the
# default Adapter for LoRA or Convpass inside the unchanged SEMA framework keeps A_N within ~2% on
# both ImageNet-A and VTAB (gaps 1.03, 1.05 on ImageNet-A; LoRA +0.59, Convpass -0.58 on VTAB),
# E04 Table 3.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Scheme family map: component_substitution lowers through component_ablation (Family 2). The
#     substitution/invariance reading is imperfect against the rule's positive-contribution
#     conclusion contributes(C, S, Q): here C = functional_adapter names the substituted component
#     slot whose contribution persists across types. The class-level generalisation ("functional
#     adapter types") is a kind-(a) absorbed scope (corpus study): the atom
#     instantiates per tested type, the claimed-class-vs-tested-set lives in nl/binding, and the
#     annotation's own coverage flag (no inductive-step construct) is recorded here, not forced
#     into vocabulary. POLICY VOCABULARY NOTE: corpus-v1 has no invariance/equivalence scheme, so
#     substitution-invariance is carried by the closest family rule + nl.
#   * Two policy-mandatory CQs are unmet, so the argument is incomplete: it is declared as a
#     located hole with `open variance_reported` (lowering re-done for issue #15 under
#     lara-core@0.3), and the claim lands `gap` on empty complete support: variance_reported (CQ3,
#     no seeds/uncertainty; gaps sit near half the 2% tolerance) and -- mapped to
#     sample_representative would need inductive_generalization, but under component_ablation the
#     scope CQ has no home, so it too stays a gap in nl. Met CQs: single_variable <- CQ1 (all SEMA
#     components but the adapter held identical); protocol_parity <- CQ1/CQ2 (both alternative
#     types on both datasets, same metrics). The 2% figure and the abs-vs-relative ambiguity live
#     in nl. Dead ends N03/N06/N12 concern expansion/routing, not adapter type -- no attacks.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact self-expansion at sha256:aa759bc10299
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not complete at corpus-v1's evidential bar -----------------

claim c04
  nl      = "SEMA generalises across functional adapter types: swapping the default Adapter for LoRA or Convpass inside the unchanged SEMA framework keeps A_N within about 2% on both ImageNet-A and VTAB (gaps 1.03 and 1.05 on ImageNet-A; LoRA +0.59 and Convpass -0.58 on VTAB)"
  formal  = contributes(functional_adapter, sema, incremental_accuracy)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the Table 3 adapter-variant cells (Adapter / LoRA / Convpass on both
# datasets), per result cell in the annotation and folded into refs.
leaf e1 : reports(e04, ablation_effect(functional_adapter, sema, incremental_accuracy, positive))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C04, evidence/tables/table3_adapter_variants.md, logic/experiments.md#E04-Procedure-step-3]

leaf e2 : isolated(functional_adapter, e04)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E04-Procedure-step-2]

leaf e3 : matched_protocol(e04)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E04-Procedure-step-1, logic/experiments.md#E04-Procedure-step-3]

# --- ... but the argument is incomplete (a located hole) ----------------------------------------

# variance_reported is open (E04 reports single-run point estimates) and mandatory, so a1 is a
# hole. The class-scope obligation has no question in component_ablation and stays in nl.
arg a1 : supports(c04) by component_ablation(functional_adapter, sema, incremental_accuracy, e04)
  discharge single_variable   with e2
  discharge protocol_parity   with e3
  open      variance_reported

status c04

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments (the hole is not a node).
# Located hole: a1, open obligations [variance_reported]; it sources no attacks.
# Claim status:
#   c04 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8;
#          the located hole is reported in `holes`, not counted as support)
